{
  "projects": {
    "default": "forge-sync"
  },

  "//": [
    "One Firebase project serves two sites, so a deploy of one cannot overwrite the other.",
    "Before this works, both sites must exist in the console (Hosting > Add another site).",
    "The names on the right are the *site* names — globally unique, and they decide the URLs:",
    "  companion -> https://<site>.web.app  (the phone PWA, companion/web)",
    "  web       -> https://<site>.web.app  (Forge Web, built from web/dist)",
    "Then, once, from companion/:",
    "  firebase target:apply hosting companion forge-sync",
    "  firebase target:apply hosting web forge-web",
    "which writes exactly the block below. See docs/forge-web.md."
  ],
  "targets": {
    "forge-sync": {
      "hosting": {
        "companion": ["forge-sync"],
        "web": ["forge-web"]
      }
    }
  }
}
